## Why This Is Asked
Tests nuanced DP on partitioning with range-dependent block costs, requiring problem decomposition, state design, and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes and block counts
- Efficient range max computation in transitions
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScore(nums, m) {
  const n = nums.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(m+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= Math.min(i, m); t++) {
      let curMax = -Infinity;
      for (let j = i-1; j >= t-1; j--) {
        curMax = Math.max(curMax, nums[j]);
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + curMax * (i - j);
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          par[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruct endpoints
  const ends = [];
  let i = n, t = m;
  while (t > 0) {
    ends.push(i);
    i = par[i][t];
    t--;
  }
  return {score: dp[n][m], ends: ends.reverse()};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests time-expanded DP on grids for path counts with constraints.

## Key Concepts
- DP on (i,j,t) layers; space optimization; modulo arithmetic.
- Handling walls and boundary checks.

## Code Example
```javascript
function countPaths(grid, k) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const MOD = 1_000_000_007;
  if (grid[0][0] === 1 || grid[n-1][m-1] === 1) return 0;
  let prev = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(m).fill(0));
  prev[0][0] = 1;
  const dirs = [[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]];
  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    const cur = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(m).fill(0));
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      if (grid[i][j] === 1) continue;
      for (const [dx,dy] of dirs) {
        const x = i + dx, y = j + dy;
        if (x>=0 && x<n && y>=0 && y<m && grid[x][y]===0) {
          cur[i][j] = (cur[i][j] + prev[x][y]) % MOD;
        }
      }
    }
    prev = cur;
  }
  return prev[n-1][m-1];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model interval scheduling with a cap on concurrent starts, a common real-world constraint in job scheduling and ad campaigns.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling with a limit on number of intervals
- Preprocessing next[i] via binary search
- DP with reconstruction pointers for actual selection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch for dp and reconstruction
function maxProfitTasks(s, d, p, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const idx = [...Array(n).keys()].sort((a,b)=> s[a]-s[b]);
  // reorder s,d,p by idx as needed; compute next[] with binary search
  const next = Array(n).fill(n);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) {
    let limit = s[i] + d[i] - 1;
    // binary search for first j with s[j] > limit
    let lo=i+1, hi=n; while (lo<hi){
      let mid=(lo+hi)>>1; if (s[mid] > limit) hi=mid; else lo=mid+1; }
    next[i] = lo;
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(false));
  for (let i=n-1;i>=0;i--) {
    for (let t=1;t<=k;t++) {
      if (dp[i+1][t] >= p[i] + dp[next[i]][t-1]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i+1][t];
        take[i][t] = false;
      } else {
        dp[i][t] = p[i] + dp[next[i]][t-1];
        take[i][t] = true;
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {profit: dp[0][k], take, next};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP with exact selection count and a non-adjacency constraint; includes reconstruction and edge handling for i-2. It also checks how to handle negative values and how to optimize space.

## Key Concepts

- 2D DP over i and t
- Non-adjacency via i-2 when taking i
- Reconstruct path from take flags
- Time/space complexity and rolling optimization

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxNonAdjacentK(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const take = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(false));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i][t], dp[i-1][t]);
      if(t>0){
        if(i>=2 && dp[i-2][t-1] !== NEG){
          const val = dp[i-2][t-1] + A[i-1];
          if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = true; }
        } else if(i===1 && dp[0][t-1] !== NEG){
          if(A[0] > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = A[0]; take[i][t] = true; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
}
```

