## Why This Is Asked
This tests DP over partitions with a non-linear block cost dependent on average, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP over k blocks
- Prefix sums for O(1) block sums
- Non-linear, floor(sum/len) cost
- Backtracking for endpoints
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const INF = 1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const sum = pref[i]-pref[p];
        const len = i-p;
        const cost = Math.floor(sum/len);
        if(dp[p][t-1] + cost < dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = dp[p][t-1] + cost;
          par[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let blocks = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const p = par[i][t];
    blocks.push([p+1, i]);
    i = p; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to optimize to faster than O(n^2 k)?
- How to handle negatives or alternative cost such as max/min?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of circular constraints with DP, case splitting, and backtracking to reconstruct indices.

## Key Concepts
- Circular-to-linear reduction via casework
- DP with two indices: position and picks left
- Backtracking to reconstruct solution
- Time/space: O(nk) both, with careful base cases

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKNonAdjCircular(A, k){
  const n=A.length;
  function solve(start, end){ /* linear range [start..end] */
    const len=end-start+1;
    const dp=Array.from({length:len+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
    const take=Array.from({length:len+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(false));
    dp[0][0]=0;
    for(let i=1;i<=len;i++){
      const val=A[start+i-1];
      for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
        // skip
        if(dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t]; }
        // take
        if(t>0){
          const cand = (i>=2?dp[i-2][t-1]: (t-1===0?0:-Infinity)) + val;
          if(cand>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=cand; take[i][t]=true; }
        }
      }
    }
    // backtrack
    let i=len, t=k, idx=[];
    while(i>0 && t>=0){
      if(take[i][t]){ idx.push(start+i-1); i-=2; t-=1; }
      else{ i-=1; }
    }
    return {sum: dp[len][k], indices: idx.reverse()};
  }
  const r1 = solve(0, n-2); // exclude A[0]
  const r2 = solve(1, n-1); // include A[0] scenario actually requires excluding end points; this is illustrative
  return r1.sum >= r2.sum ? r1 : r2;
}
```

